---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Pic from '../../components/Pic.astro';
import PostCard from '../../components/PostCard.astro';
import CTABand from '../../components/CTABand.astro';
import Share from '../../components/Share.astro';
import { posts } from '../../data/posts';
import { tel, phone } from '../../data/site';
const toc = [['short', 'The short answer'], ['how', 'How each system works'], ['questions', 'Three questions we ask'], ['which', 'So, which one?']];
const rows = [['Rooms covered', 'Whole home, zoned', 'One room per indoor unit'], ['Visible inside', 'Ceiling outlets only', 'Wall unit per room'], ['Upfront cost', '$X,XXX–$XX,XXX [sample]', '$X,XXX per room [sample]'], ['Install time', '1–2 days', 'Half a day per unit']];
const more = [posts[0], posts[1], posts[5]];
const p = 'text-[17px] leading-[1.7] text-[#2f3a40] sm:text-[18px]';
---
<Base title="Ducted vs Split Systems: Which Suits a Melbourne Home? | Cooper & Vale" description="The honest trade-offs in cost, comfort and looks between ducted reverse cycle and split systems — and the three questions we ask." active="blog">
  <article>
    <header class="bg-cream">
      <div class="wrap pt-12 lg:pt-16">
        <div class="max-w-[880px]">
          <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-[13px] text-muted"><a href="/" class="hover:text-ink">Home</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><a href="/blog/" class="hover:text-ink">Blog</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><span aria-current="page">Comparisons</span></nav>
          <p class="mt-6 text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.08em] text-teal-dark uppercase">Comparisons</p>
          <h1 class="mt-3 text-[36px] leading-[1.1] sm:text-[56px]">Ducted vs split systems: which suits a Melbourne home?</h1>
          <p class="mt-5 text-[18px] leading-relaxed text-muted sm:text-[20px]">The honest trade-offs in cost, comfort and looks — and the three questions we ask before recommending either.</p>
          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4 border-t border-line pt-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="grid size-12 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ink font-display text-[16px] text-peach">PV</span><div><p class="text-[15px] font-bold">Priya Vale</p><p class="text-[13px] text-muted">Co-founder &amp; system designer [sample]  ·  12 Oct 2026  ·  8 min read</p></div></div>
            <Share />
          </div>
        </div>
        <Pic name="cosy1" alt="Warm living room with ducted outlets (sample imagery)" class="mt-10 aspect-[32/15] w-full" sizes="(min-width:1440px) 1280px, 100vw" widths={[640, 1280, 1920]} eager />
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="bg-cream">
      <div class="wrap grid gap-12 py-14 lg:grid-cols-[316px_760px] lg:gap-20 lg:py-20">
        <aside class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start">
          <p class="eyebrow">In this article</p>
          <ol class="mt-4 border-t border-line">{toc.map(([id, t], i) => <li class="border-b border-line"><a href={`#${id}`} class="flex gap-3 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium hover:text-copper-dark"><span class="text-[13px] text-copper">0{i + 1}</span>{t}</a></li>)}</ol>
          <div class="mt-8 rounded-[2px] bg-ink p-6 text-white">
            <p class="font-display text-[22px] leading-snug">Not sure which suits your home?</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[14px] text-stone-2">We'll compare both in your home, in writing.</p>
            <a href="/contact/#consult" class="btn btn-copper btn-sm mt-5 w-full">Book a Free Consult</a>
            <a href={tel} class="mt-3 block text-center text-[13px] text-peach">or call {phone}</a>
          </div>
        </aside>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <p class="font-display text-[21px] leading-snug sm:text-[24px]">If you're heating and cooling a Melbourne home, you'll almost always end up choosing between ducted reverse cycle and split systems. Both are reverse cycle — they heat and cool — but they solve different problems.</p>
          <h2 id="short" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 text-[28px] sm:text-[32px]">The short answer</h2>
          <p class={`mt-4 ${p}`}>Ducted suits whole-home comfort, three or more bedrooms and people who don't want units on the walls. Splits suit homes that need one to three rooms done well, have little roof access, or want the lowest upfront cost.</p>
          <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full min-w-[520px] text-left text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-ink text-white"><tr><th class="px-4 py-3">System</th><th class="px-4 py-3">Ducted reverse cycle</th><th class="px-4 py-3">Split systems</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>{rows.map(([a, b, c], i) => <tr class={i % 2 ? 'bg-white' : 'bg-cream'}><th class="px-4 py-3 font-bold">{a}</th><td class="px-4 py-3">{b}</td><td class="px-4 py-3">{c}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
          </table></div>
          <h2 id="how" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 text-[28px] sm:text-[32px]">How each system works</h2>
          <p class={`mt-4 ${p}`}>A ducted system has one indoor fan coil in your roof space, connected to an outdoor unit. Insulated ducts carry air to outlets in each room, and zones let you choose which rooms get it.</p>
          <p class={`mt-4 ${p}`}>A split system puts an indoor unit on the wall of each room, piped to an outdoor unit. Multi-head systems run several indoor units from one outdoor unit.</p>
          <blockquote class="mt-10 border-l-[3px] border-copper pl-6"><p class="font-display text-[24px] leading-snug sm:text-[28px]">“The right system is the one sized and placed for your house — not the biggest box on the quote.”</p><footer class="mt-3 text-[14px] text-muted">— Priya Vale</footer></blockquote>
          <h2 id="questions" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 text-[28px] sm:text-[32px]">Three questions we ask</h2>
          <ol class="mt-6 space-y-5">{['How many rooms do you actually use, and when?', "What's in the roof space — and can we get to it?", 'Are you replacing gas heating (and could VEU discounts apply) [sample]?'].map((q, i) => <li class="flex gap-4 text-[17px] sm:text-[18px]"><span class="font-display text-[24px] leading-none text-copper">{i + 1}</span>{q}</li>)}</ol>
          <figure class="mt-10"><Pic name="thermo2" alt="Ducted zoning wall controller (sample imagery)" class="aspect-[76/42] w-full" sizes="(min-width:1024px) 760px, 100vw" /><figcaption class="mt-3 text-[14px] text-muted">Ducted zoning is controlled from one wall controller or an app. Sample imagery.</figcaption></figure>
          <h2 id="which" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 text-[28px] sm:text-[32px]">So, which one?</h2>
          <p class={`mt-4 ${p}`}>If you want the whole house comfortable and nothing on the walls, ducted is usually worth it. If you need a couple of rooms sorted quickly and affordably, splits are hard to beat. Most of our consults end with a written comparison of both.</p>
          <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-4 border-y border-line py-5 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between"><p class="text-[15px] text-muted">Found this useful? Share it with someone weighing up the same decision.</p><Share /></div>
          <div class="mt-8 flex gap-5 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8"><span class="grid size-14 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ink font-display text-[22px] text-peach">PV</span><div><p class="font-display text-[22px]">Written by Priya Vale</p><p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">Priya co-founded Cooper &amp; Vale and leads system design. She has spent 15+ years designing heating and cooling for Melbourne homes [sample].</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="wrap sec">
      <div class="flex items-end justify-between gap-4"><h2 class="h2">Keep reading</h2><a href="/blog/" class="link-arrow shrink-0">All articles&nbsp; →</a></div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">{more.map((x) => <PostCard p={x} small />)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CTABand title="Want us to compare both in your home?" sub="Free in-home consult. Ducted and split options, side by side, in writing." />
</Base>
